  "result": "I couldn't find a past ticket that reports this same problem.\n\n- **PowerToys#48774:** Closest. It covers a Power Display profile that doesn't switch on wake when it's linked to Light Switch. Your problem is the reverse: a profile you set yourself changes on wake.\n- **PowerToys#47951:** Power Display stops working after sleep or hibernate. That ticket has no detail.\n- **PowerToys#47776:** Monitor-specific settings reset after the monitor is turned off and on. That's a different symptom.\n\nPlease file this as a new bug and attach a bug report ZIP from PowerToys. Say that you use a USB-C dock with two monitors, and that the active profile changes after wake. As a stopgap, you could manually re-apply your dimmed profile after waking, or check whether Light Switch is set to switch Power Display profiles. Those are my guesses, not fixes confirmed in the archive.\n\n```json\n{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no past ticket reporting this exact problem. The closest is PowerToys#48774, where a Light Switch-linked profile doesn't trigger on wake. That is a different problem. Please file this as a new bug with a bug report ZIP, and mention the USB-C dock with two monitors and the profile change on wake. As a stopgap, re-apply your dimmed profile manually after waking, or check whether Light Switch is set to switch Power Display profiles. Those are my suggestions, not fixes confirmed in the archive.\"}\n```",
